"Industry context
Microsoft 365 Copilot trend: mainstream-scaling; driver: Microsoft 365 Copilot Wave 2 (September 2024) — Pages, Python in Excel, redesigned Business Chat — followed by Ignite 2024 autonomous agents announcements and Build 2024 Team Copilot disclosures. (Microsoft — "Microsoft 365 Copilot Wave 2: Pages, Python in Excel, and agents" (Jared Spataro), 2024-09). Metrics: global_knowledge_workers_using_genai_at_work: 75% of global knowledge workers reporting they use generative AI at work (Microsoft and LinkedIn Work Trend Index Annual Report 2024 — "AI at Work Is Here. Now Comes the Hard Part.", 2024-05); genai_use_growth_year_over_year: 46-75% point growth: 46% in 2023 to 75% in 2024 of knowledge workers using AI at work (Microsoft and LinkedIn Work Trend Index Annual Report 2024, 2024-05). Patterns: in-app-copilot-side-pane: Users invoke Copilot inside Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, and OneNote via the side pane or ribbon. This is the default deployment surface — drafting, summarising, rewriting, and editing inside the document the user is already in. (Microsoft and LinkedIn Work Trend Index Annual Report 2024, 2024-05) business-chat-graph-grounded: Business Chat ("Copilot Chat" in the Microsoft 365 app and Teams) reasons over the tenant's Microsoft Graph — emails, files, chats, calendars — to answer questions and produce content grounded in the user's own data. Microsoft renamed and expanded this surface in the Wave 2 update. (Microsoft — "Microsoft 365 Copilot Wave 2: Pages, Python in Excel, and agents" (Jared Spataro), 2024-09) Industry context refreshed 2026-05-30."
